+that @c tf::ObjectPool relies on — @c allocate, @c deallocate and @c release —
+with the same observable behaviour: a mutex-protected free list of recycled
+blocks that is grown in chunks of @c blocks_per_chunk blocks, so a single lock
+acquisition amortises over a whole chunk. Unlike @c synchronized_pool_resource,
+which maintains one pool per rounded-up block size, this pool serves a single
+block size; requests larger than that (or more strictly aligned) bypass the
+pool and go straight to @c ::operator new / @c ::operator delete.
